{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-25T23:28:25.276Z","data":{"text":"Both gates are green. Summary:\n\n**Task 4 — Mutation check after a pass**\n\n- **`src/watcher/mutation-check.ts`** (new): `runMutationCheck` reads the task's latest start/end `measures` views, builds the scenario index once, picks via `pickMutations`, and runs picks in order through `runMutationPick` under one `budgetSeconds` wall-clock budget (each run's timeout = budget left). It appends one `mutation_ran` event per pick with all required fields; unknown ranges are `range_unknown`, picks left after the budget are `budget`, and `command_failed`/`timed_out` carry bounded output. All errors are caught and logged, never touching the task state.\n- **`src/watcher/loop.ts`**: one `runMutationCheck(...)` call in the `taskResult.success` branch, before `archiveCompletedSpec`.\n- **`tests/mutation-check.test.ts`** (new): 7 tests driving real watcher cycles with a mutating fake adapter and a fake `node` mutation command, covering the two required scenarios plus the broken-command case, helper ranges, test-only picks, `range_unknown`, `report_invalid`, budget exhaustion (`timed_out` then `budget`), and mutation unset.\n\nVerification:\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/mutation-check.test.ts` → 7/7 pass\n- `pnpm verify` → exit 0\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/083-traceability-mutation/.run/results/4.md`."}}
